model {
  extend basalt.catalog {
    metadata {
      constraint "Catalog connection guidance binds exact requirement and method names without changing credential identity. The identity provider's management sign-in and retained API-key provider use separate credentials and require approval for every mutation; switching methods offers only declared, same-scope requirements the server allows the caller to connect. Local and hosted forms share reversible choices and preserve the shared OAuth-first default unless a method was explicitly chosen. Provider denial descriptions survive across app, onboarding and local recovery, including access-denied refusals. Only the authorized callback tab's exact current target can show an ephemeral service refusal and reopen normal connection choices. Unmerged guidance context composes with account-identity imports; the maintained identity-provider publisher pins the served framework while its published snapshot stays frozen. Relative setup paths resolve against the selected HTTPS account site, never the dashboard origin."
    }
  }
}
